  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Since there's a lot of avatar creators that want to make transforming and size-changing avatars, something like secondhand view positions for animation could help a ton. You could have your main viewball, and then have multiple secondhand viewballs that you could switch to seeing through via animation, all still locked on the avatar's head and everything. The main viewball can be what you see through when your ingame menu's open, or when you reset your avatar etc. Yknow, being a /main/ viewball. probably don't need to type out the explanation this long, but my point is it'd be awesome and a good alternative to the not-too-workable concept of a viewball that can change positions, and would be a ton of help to creators that want the avatars to do the size change thing. \nLike me. \n...I'm selfish.",
